{{ 'character-page.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{%- comment -%}
  Alterpop — Character header. Source of truth: Wireframe 9a (Character Page).
  Renders on templates/metaobject/character.json — the `character` metaobject's
  own storefront template. Current entry is the `metaobject` global.

  Decalque of sections/line-header.liquid (Phase 5 rework of the Line page),
  same structure, swapped for the metaobject fields resolved 17/09/2026:
    H1                  -> metaobject.title.value
    subtitle (universe)  -> metaobject.universe.value | first -> .title
    piece count          -> non-blank entries of metaobject.products.value
                            (0 -> the meta line is not rendered)

  Only 4 fields exist on the `character` metaobject definition today: title,
  image, universe (list.collection_reference), products
  (list.product_reference). No artwork/franchise/description/related_characters
  field exists — do not invent one. `image` is confirmed unused by 9a and is
  intentionally not read here (see character-grid.liquid's "Pendente a
  reportar" note).

  Breadcrumb "Home / {Universe} / {Character}" — Universe is
  metaobject.universe (list.collection_reference); its first entry's .url/.title
  come straight off the referenced Collection. No Universe reference on this
  character -> that crumb collapses (Home / Character), never a placeholder.

  Meta line is figure count ONLY. The wireframe's "N figures · min–maxcm ·
  minYear–maxYear" is NOT reproduced: there is no year field anywhere on
  Product, and ociostock.dimensions is a full package L×W×H string (e.g.
  "20 × 18 × 18 cm"), not a single comparable height — aggregating a min/max
  range from it would mean guessing which of the three numbers is height.
  Reported, not built. Count uses the existing 'sections.catalogue.count_figures'
  locale key (matches wireframe wording "N figures in catalog"), pluralised.

  Enters with the shared editorial animation (ap-editorial-in, 400ms;
  neutralised under prefers-reduced-motion in tokens.css) — same as
  line-header.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  # `.first` (property accessor) returns null on this metaobject
  # list.collection_reference drop, even though the field genuinely holds a
  # value and `| json` shows a proper array — confirmed against the live
  # Luffy entry (universe: One Piece) on 18/09/2026. The `first` FILTER
  # works. Use the filter form for any metaobject list-reference field.
  assign ap_universe = metaobject.universe.value | first
  # Count what the grid can render, not array entries: .size also counts dead
  # (blank) references, and "13 figures" over 12 cards is a visible lie.
  # Same rule as the loops in character-grid.liquid; a `render` would isolate
  # scope, so the few lines are repeated on purpose rather than shared.
  assign ap_figure_count = 0
  for product in metaobject.products.value
    if product == blank
      continue
    endif
    assign ap_figure_count = ap_figure_count | plus: 1
  endfor
  # `title` is required on the definition, so this fallback should never fire;
  # it is a net so a blank title can't leave an empty H1 / breadcrumb / aria-label.
  assign ap_title = metaobject.title.value | default: metaobject.system.handle
-%}

<section class="ap-character-header" aria-label="{{ ap_title | escape }}">
  <div class="ap-character-header__inner page-width">
    <nav class="ap-character-header__crumbs type-caption" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="{{ routes.root_url }}">{{ 'sections.catalogue.home' | t }}</a>
      {%- if ap_universe != blank -%}
        <span aria-hidden="true">&rsaquo;</span>
        <a href="{{ ap_universe.url }}">{{ ap_universe.title | escape }}</a>
      {%- endif -%}
      <span aria-hidden="true">&rsaquo;</span>
      <span aria-current="page">{{ ap_title | escape }}</span>
    </nav>

    <h1 class="ap-character-header__title type-display">{{ ap_title | escape | upcase }}</h1>

    {%- if ap_universe != blank -%}
      <p class="ap-character-header__universe type-body">{{ ap_universe.title | escape }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if ap_figure_count > 0 -%}
      <p class="ap-character-header__meta type-caption" data-ap-slot="figures-count">
        {{ 'sections.catalogue.count_figures' | t: count: ap_figure_count }}
      </p>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</section>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Character header",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "section",
  "settings": [],
  "enabled_on": {
    "templates": ["metaobject"]
  }
}
{% endschema %}
